  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nStout dome of high pressure will build over the southern states\nthis weekend, eventually moving overhead Tuesday through\nThursday. This ridge pattern and bubble of high pressure will\nkeep the area mostly dry for the next few days, save for an\nisolated thunderstorm chance across the mountains Sunday\nafternoon and maybe Monday evening with shortwave disturbances.\n\nThe main feature for the next several days will be the\nincreasing heat and humidity. High temperatures across the\nlowlands today and Sunday will be in the mid 80s to lower 90s.\nThese temperatures will increase next week with guidance\nsuggesting Tuesday through Thursday will have areas of the \nlowlands reaching the mid to upper 90s. Dew points in the upper\n60s and lower 70s will create dangerous heat index values in the\nupper 90s and lower 100s. Will have to monitor these trends for\npotential heat advisory issuance mid week.",
